abstract: "Official Python implementation of VESTA (Variance-Evaluated Stability for Transit Analysis), a depth-invariant, variance-stabilized transit vetting framework benchmarked across four decades in Kepler light curves (N=56 population). Submitted to Astronomy and Computing."
